Original license: licenses/nunif.txt
UPSTREAM.json records original source-file hashes and extracted destinations.

Copied portions: iw3/forward_warp.py, iw3/dilation.py,
iw3/models/light_inpaint_v1.py, iw3/models/depth_aa.py,
and the nunif/modules attention, normalization, initialization, permutation,
padding, Gaussian-filter and compile helpers needed by those two models.
Non-inference standalone benchmarks/tests are stripped. Imports point to this
pack's private vendor package. Model registration/metadata use a minimal local
base instead of the full nunif model registry; tensor inference is unchanged.
core.py adapts iw3/base_inpaint.py and iw3/forward_inpaint.py's still-image mask,
eye-orientation and model-inference sequence, and iw3's DA3 depth processing.

Only official release model artifacts are downloaded. No weights are included
in the distributable archive. Upstream publishes these two models with the MIT
repository and does not state a separate license for them in the inspected
release/model sources. The noncommercial warnings in iw3's README concern
specified third-party depth models, which this pack does not download or bundle.
An existing user's DA3 model retains its own terms independently.

Design/reference inspection only; no code copied from these repositories:
https://github.com/Dobidop/ComfyStereo (MIT)
https://github.com/enoky/resolve-iw3 (MIT)
https://github.com/SamSeenX/ComfyUI_SSStereoscope

resolve-iw3's stereo_inpaint.py and tests implement monobw_inpaint and MLBW
pipelines, not the requested forward_inpaint warp. Its LightInpaintV1 checkpoint
and directional-mask approach were useful cross-checks, but its warp was not
adopted. Its inspected docs/tests refer to a local nunif checkout and do not
record an exact upstream commit pin; no revision parity is inferred from that.

All repository revisions inspected are recorded in UPSTREAM.json. ComfyUI core
source was inspected locally to integrate DA3 and model management; no core
ComfyUI code is redistributed as part of this pack.
